{"type":"text","timestamp":1794547461762,"sessionID":"ses_e2ca66d86ffeQHDVXGxsL6fzIZ","part":{"id":"prt_1d35d21a8001qkRsfbaPps9Mch","sessionID":"ses_e2ca66d86ffeQHDVXGxsL6fzIZ","messageID":"msg_1d35d18c000112EpJW19CDpZ64","type":"text","text":"T028 done. Both named files changed, verify green.\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`\n  - Exported `offerSeenIn(events, expectedCommand)`: filters `commandLines(events)` through `namesCommand`, returns `{ offerSeen, commandState }` from the last matching line, and `{ offerSeen: false, commandState: null }` when the expected command is empty.\n  - `scoreRun` now carries `offerSeen` and `commandState` (JSDoc updated).\n  - `newTally` / `tallyBlock` gained `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined`; `addScored` counts a seen offer on any scored row and a `declined` command state.\n  - Text summary now prints `offer seen <n>, declined <n>`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`\n  - Added the `offerSeenIn` describe with the declined-on-expected-command case (including `startState(...).started === false`) and the wrong-command case.\n  - Added the summary case: `SUMMARY_ROW` on the fixture session gives `offerSeen: 1, offerDeclined: 0`.\n\n**Verify** (`VT` = `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` in `ADV`):\n\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  55 passed (55)\n```\n\n**Additional checks run**\n- `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` → exit 0.\n- `node --check` on the scorer → exit 0.\n- Non-JSON summary smoke run over `runs-g2.jsonl`: prints `offer seen 0, declined 0`.\n\n**Not done**\n- Did not tick T028 in `tasks.md`, per instruction.\n- Nothing blocked. No git state touched.","time":{"start":1794547458472,"end":1794547461762}}}
